{
  "gate": "arc-a770-layout-20261126",
  "title": "Arc A770: the packed GEMV's read pattern against a 256-row blocked layout, with the decode removed",
  "measured": "2026-11-26",
  "commit": "unreleased",
  "command": "python bench-logs/arc_layout_probe.py --device-name Arc --reps 7",
  "notes": "The 2.5 27B's 401 ternary matrices, 6,799,564,800 bytes per token, distinct bytes in two 3.76 GiB chunks, one persistent launch per chunk at parts=1 and grid 1 MiB. Two address layouts over the same bytes (the pack's own [phase][slot][row], and a repacked [tile][phase][slot][row] with 256-row tiles) and the same two patterns with the decode removed, 7 samples per arm per cycle over two cycles, medians with ranges. The repack is a device pass timed separately as a load-time cost. Not a model run: attention, norms, GDN, the f32 head work and the KV cache are excluded, and there is no Intel backend or support claim. The harness is bench-logs/arc_layout_probe.py, which is not tracked.",
